„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§and there they burnt incense in all the high places, as did the heathen whom the LORD carried away before them; and wrought wicked things to provoke the LORD to anger:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWfor they served idols, whereof the LORD had said unto them, Ye shall not do this thing.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ!Yet the LORD testified against Israel, and against Judah, by all the prophets, and by all the seers, saying, Turn ye from your evil ways, and keep my commandments and my statutes, according to all the law which I commanded your fathers, and which I sent to you by my servants the prophets.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNotwithstanding they would not hear, but hardened their necks, like to the neck of their fathers, that did not believe in the LORD their God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ6And they rejected his statutes, and his covenant that he made with their fathers, and his testimonies which he testified against them; and they followed vanity, and became vain, and went after the heathen that were round about them, concerning whom the LORD had charged them, that they should not do like them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ±And they left all the commandments of the LORD their God, and made them molten images, even two calves, and made a grove, and worshipped all the host of heaven, and served Baal.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÀAnd they caused their sons and their daughters to pass through the fire, and used divination and enchantments, and sold themselves to do evil in the sight of the LORD, to provoke him to anger.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚Therefore the LORD was very angry with Israel, and removed them out of his sight: there was none left but the tribe of Judah only.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAlso Judah kept not the commandments of the LORD their God, but walked in the statutes of Israel which they made.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜And the LORD rejected all the seed of Israel, and afflicted them, and delivered them into the hand of spoilers, until he had cast them out of his sight.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«For he rent Israel from the house of David; and they made Jeroboam the son of Nebat king: and Jeroboam drave Israel from following the LORD, and made them sin a great sin.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhFor the children of Israel walked in all the sins of Jeroboam which he did; they departed not from them;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«until the LORD removed Israel out of his sight, as he had said by all his servants the prophets. So was Israel carried away out of their own land to Assyria unto this day.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÿAnd the king of Assyria brought men from Babylon, and from Cuthah, and from Ava, and from Hamath, and from Sepharvaim, and placed them in the cities of Samaria instead of the children of Israel: and they possessed Samaria, and dwelt in the cities thereof.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™And so it was at the beginning of their dwelling there, that they feared not the LORD: therefore the LORD sent lions among them, which slew some of them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ)Wherefore they spake to the king of Assyria, saying, The nations which thou hast removed, and placed in the cities of Samaria, know not the manner of the God of the land: therefore he hath sent lions among them, and, behold, they slay them, because they know not the manner of the God of the land.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÄThen the king of Assyria commanded, saying, Carry thither one of the priests whom ye brought from thence; and let them go and dwell there, and let him teach them the manner of the God of the land.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰Then one of the priests whom they had carried away from Samaria came and dwelt in Beth-el, and taught them how they should fear the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªHowbeit every nation made gods of their own, and put them in the houses of the high places which the Samaritans had made, every nation in their cities wherein they dwelt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoAnd the men of Babylon made Succoth-benoth, and the men of Cuth made Nergal, and the men of Hamath made Ashima,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙand the Avites made Nibhaz and Tartak, and the Sepharvites burnt their children in fire to Adrammelech and Anammelech, the gods of Sepharvaim.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸSo they feared the LORD, and made unto themselves of the lowest of them priests of the high places, which sacrificed for them in the houses of the high places.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtThey feared the LORD, and served their own gods, after the manner of the nations whom they carried away from thence.¦layout ªlast_verse!…¤book§chapter«first_verse"ªlast_verse)¦verses˜„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙïUnto this day they do after the former manners: they fear not the LORD, neither do they after their statutes, or after their ordinances, or after the law and commandment which the LORD commanded the children of Jacob, whom he named Israel;¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢with whom the LORD had made a covenant, and charged them, saying, Ye shall not fear other gods, nor bow yourselves to them, nor serve them, nor sacrifice to them:¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ²but the LORD, who brought you up out of the land of Egypt with great power and a stretched out arm, him shall ye fear, and him shall ye worship, and to him shall ye do sacrifice.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¦And the statutes, and the ordinances, and the law, and the commandment, which he wrote for you, ye shall observe to do for evermore; and ye shall not fear other gods.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd the covenant that I have made with you ye shall not forget; neither shall ye fear other gods.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbBut the LORD your God ye shall fear; and he shall deliver you out of the hand of all your enemies.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEHowbeit they did not hearken, but they did after their former manner.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥So these nations feared the LORD, and served their graven images, both their children, and their children's children: as did their fathers, so do they unto this day.¦layout ªlast_verse)